; ======================================================================
; pi4WifiPmk.pi4 - DERIVE THE PMK FOR EVERY STORED NETWORK AND LEAVE IT
; IN DRAM FOR THE JOIN PAYLOAD TO PICK UP. RESUMABLE.
;
; DIAGNOSTIC. Does not ship.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
; WHY THIS IS A SEPARATE PAYLOAD, AND WHY IT RESUMES.
;
; MEASURED ON SILICON. pi4WifiJoin.pi4 used to run
; nine published crypto vectors before touching the radio, on the
; estimate that two 4096-iteration derivations would cost "tens of
; milliseconds apiece". The board printed:
;
;     -- the supplicant crypto, published vectors --
;       ... all nine ok ...
;       elapsed ms         15497
;
; and then the deadman fired. FIFTEEN AND A HALF SECONDS, with the
; radio still cold. Roughly ten of those seconds are ONE
; passphrase-to-PSK mapping: PBKDF2-SHA1 at 4096 iterations over two
; output blocks is 16,384 HMAC-SHA1 calls, and with the MMU off every
; instruction fetch and every load is uncached Device memory.
;
; The watchdog on this part cannot be armed past ~15.999 s
; (PM_WDOG_MAX_TICKS $000FFFFF, safety.pi4) and a payload must not arm
; its own - pi4NeonLiar.pi4:2514 records what that costs: Anvil stops
; the watchdog IT armed when the payload returns and never learns about
; ours, so the board resets after every run. So the ceiling is fifteen
; seconds, full stop, and four networks at ten seconds each do not fit
; in one run any more than they fit inside the join.
;
; THEREFORE: this payload does as many derivations as fit, writes them
; to a fixed DRAM window, and RUNS AGAIN to do the rest. Each run
; reports how many are staged and how many are still owed. When it says
; "all staged", run the join.
;
; ======================================================================
; WHAT TO TYPE
; ======================================================================
;     pmf> fill 1400000 0 800
;     pmf> load SETTINGS.TXT 1400000
;     pmf> deadman 15
;     pmf> map              <- it prints `stage a file at <stage>`. An
;                              image is the same bytes at any --load-addr.
;     pmf> run <stage>       <- repeat until it says all staged
;
; The three radio blobs are NOT needed here; this payload never touches
; the bus. Only SETTINGS.TXT, and only because that is where the
; passphrase lives.
;
; ======================================================================
; NOTHING DERIVED FROM THE PASSPHRASE OR THE PMK IS EVER PRINTED
; ======================================================================
; Not the passphrase, not the PMK, not a hash of the PMK, not one byte
; of it. What is printed is the SSID, the passphrase's LENGTH and the
; milliseconds each derivation took - enough to tell "it worked" from
; "that slot has no credential", and nothing anyone could use.
;
; THE PMK IS AS GOOD AS THE PASSPHRASE. Anyone holding those 32 bytes
; joins this network for as long as the passphrase stands; it is not a
; "derived, therefore safe" value. That is why the window is DRAM the
; next payload reads and why this file has no dump command.
; ======================================================================

; THE SETTINGS STORE NAMES NO OTHER FILE - a library never
; includes a library - so ITS dependencies are listed here, in this order,
; by the main program. Anvil/Core/settings.pbi is chip-free core and
; reaches a medium only through the HwFile* seam: Anvil/Hal/hal.pbi
; declares that seam's #HW_FILE_* codes, and Anvil/Storage/hwfile.pbi
; is THIS board's backend for it, written over fat.pi4. Both come before
; the store, exactly as the store's own USE block and
; pi4SettingsSelfTest.pi4 have it. hal.pbi's RequireCap prints a refusal
; and so names Print/PrintN/UartWriteStr, which is why uart.pi4 stays
; first.
;
; This program only ever calls SettingsParse() against the window Anvil's
; `load` filled, so none of that machinery ever executes here - but a file
; is compiled whole and every name in it has to resolve.
;
; LOSING THESE TWO LINES IS WHAT STOPPED THIS PROGRAM BUILDING. The store
; moved out of RaspberryPi4/Lib and onto the seam; the XIncludeFile
; below was given its new path and nothing
; else was added, so #HW_FILE_OK resolved nowhere in this translation
; unit. The monitor (RaspberryPi4/Board/board.pi4) and the settings gate
; (pi4SettingsSelfTest.pi4) both already listed the two files, which is
; why the identical library built there and only these two diagnostics
; broke. tools/a64/a64_diag_build_check.py builds every diagnostic in
; this directory so the next such omission is caught the same day.
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/uart.pi4"
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/timer.pi4"
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/fat.pi4"
XIncludeFile "Anvil/Hal/hal.pbi"
XIncludeFile "Anvil/Core/wallclock.pbi"            ; hwfile.pbi stamps changes with it
XIncludeFile "Anvil/Storage/hwfile.pbi"
XIncludeFile "Anvil/Core/settings.pbi"
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/sha1.pi4"
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/hmacsha1.pi4"
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/pbkdf2.pi4"

; Where Anvil's `load` put SETTINGS.TXT, and the size of the zeroed
; window in front of it. pi4WifiJoin.pi4's numbers, unchanged: a second
; opinion about where the file lives is a second thing to get wrong.
#SET_ADDR = $01400000
#SET_WIN  = 8192

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  THE STAGING WINDOW at $01500000, clear of everything else this bench
;  uses - firmware $01000000, NVRAM $01200000 with its work area at
;  $01210000, scratch $01220000, CLM $01300000, settings $01400000.
;
;      +0   4   magic        $504D4B31, 'P' 'M' 'K' '1'
;      +4   4   count        entries that follow
;      +8   4   fingerprint  FNV-1a over the whole settings text
;      +12  4   reserved
;      +16  ..  entries, #PMKS_ENTRY bytes each
;
;  and each entry is
;
;      +0   4   slot         the settings slot it came from
;      +4   4   ssidLen      1..32
;      +8  32   ssid         raw bytes, NOT terminated
;      +40 32   pmk          the 32 bytes
;      +72  8   pad
;
;  THE FINGERPRINT IS WHAT MAKES RESUMING SAFE. Without it a window
;  staged from yesterday's SETTINGS.TXT would be reused after somebody
;  changed a passphrase at the console, and the join would fail its
;  message 3 MIC with no visible cause. Any change to the file at all -
;  including a comment - invalidates the whole window and starts again,
;  which is the cheap and obviously-correct rule rather than the clever
;  one.
;
;  MATCHED BY SSID AT THE FAR END, not by slot. The slot is carried for
;  a person reading a log; the join picks by the SSID it chose, because
;  the ladder can pick a network in a different order from the one
;  settings stores it in and a slot index would pair the wrong key with
;  the right name.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#PMKS_ADDR      = $01500000
#PMKS_MAGIC     = $504D4B31
#PMKS_HDR       = 16
#PMKS_OFF_COUNT = 4
#PMKS_OFF_FP    = 8
#PMKS_ENTRY     = 80
#PMKS_OFF_SLOT  = 0
#PMKS_OFF_SLEN  = 4
#PMKS_OFF_SSID  = 8
#PMKS_OFF_PMK   = 40
#PMKS_MAX       = 8

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  HOW LATE A DERIVATION MAY BE STARTED.
;
;  One measured derivation is about ten seconds and the deadman is
;  fifteen. Starting one at t = 4000 ms therefore finishes at about
;  14 000 ms, which leaves a second for the report; starting one at
;  t = 6000 ms does not. The number is a START gate rather than a
;  deadline because there is no way to stop a derivation once it is
;  running - PBKDF2 has no yield - so the only honest control is
;  refusing to begin.
;
;  IF THE MEASURED COST CHANGES, THIS IS THE NUMBER THAT MOVES. It is
;  printed on every run beside the actual elapsed time so the two can
;  be compared without reading the source.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#PMKS_START_BY_MS = 4000

Global g_hz.i = 0

Procedure PutHexN(v.i, digits.i)
  Define i.i
  Define n.i
  For i = digits - 1 To 0 Step -1
    n = (v >> (i * 4)) & $F
    If n < 10
      UartWrite(48 + n)
    Else
      UartWrite(55 + n)
    EndIf
  Next
EndProcedure

Procedure Line(*name, v.i)
  UartWriteStr("  ")
  UartWriteStr(*name)
  UartWriteStr("  ")
  PrintDec(v)
  PrintNl()
  UartDrain()
EndProcedure

; An SSID is 32 arbitrary bytes chosen by whoever runs the access point.
; Everything outside printable ASCII is replaced, so a name carrying
; escape sequences cannot rewrite the lines above it in a log destined
; for a report. pi4WifiJoin.pi4's PrintSsid; the duplication is
; deliberate, these payloads share no code by design.
Procedure PrintSsid(p.i, n.i)
  Define j.i
  If n <= 0
    UartWriteStr("<hidden>")
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  If n > 32
    n = 32
  EndIf
  For j = 0 To n - 1
    If PeekA(p + j) >= 32 And PeekA(p + j) <= 126
      UartWrite(PeekA(p + j))
    Else
      UartWrite(46)
    EndIf
  Next
EndProcedure

Procedure.i MsSince(t0.i)
  If g_hz <= 0
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  ProcedureReturn ((Ticks() - t0) * 1000) / g_hz
EndProcedure

; FNV-1a, 32 bits, over the settings text. NOT a security function and
; it is not asked to be one: it answers "is this the same file as last
; run", where the alternative to a wrong answer is a re-derivation, not
; a break-in. Masked to 32 bits at every step because .i here is 64.
Procedure.i Fnv1a(p.i, n.i)
  Define h.i
  Define i.i
  h = $811C9DC5
  For i = 0 To n - 1
    h = (h ! PeekA(p + i)) & $FFFFFFFF
    h = (h * 16777619) & $FFFFFFFF
  Next
  ProcedureReturn h
EndProcedure

Procedure.i Rd32(p.i)
  ProcedureReturn PeekA(p) | (PeekA(p + 1) << 8) | (PeekA(p + 2) << 16) | (PeekA(p + 3) << 24)
EndProcedure

Procedure Wr32(p.i, v.i)
  PokeB(p + 0, v & $FF)
  PokeB(p + 1, (v >> 8) & $FF)
  PokeB(p + 2, (v >> 16) & $FF)
  PokeB(p + 3, (v >> 24) & $FF)
EndProcedure

; Is this SSID already in the staged table? Returns 1 or 0.
Procedure.i AlreadyStaged(count.i, ssid.i, ssidLen.i)
  Define e.i
  Define ent.i
  Define k.i
  Define same.i
  For e = 0 To count - 1
    ent = #PMKS_ADDR + #PMKS_HDR + e * #PMKS_ENTRY
    If Rd32(ent + #PMKS_OFF_SLEN) = ssidLen
      same = 1
      For k = 0 To ssidLen - 1
        If PeekA(ent + #PMKS_OFF_SSID + k) <> PeekA(ssid + k)
          same = 0
        EndIf
      Next
      If same = 1
        ProcedureReturn 1
      EndIf
    EndIf
  Next
  ProcedureReturn 0
EndProcedure

Procedure.i Main()
  Define i.i
  Define ok.i
  Define setLen.i
  Define slot.i
  Define ssid.i
  Define ssidLen.i
  Define pass.i
  Define passLen.i
  Define count.i
  Define fp.i
  Define oldFp.i
  Define t.i
  Define took.i
  Define ent.i
  Define tRun.i
  Define usable.i
  Define derived.i
  Define owed.i

  If TimerInit() <> 0
    g_hz = TickHz()
  EndIf
  tRun = Ticks()

  PrintNl()
  UartWriteStr("=== pi4WifiPmk - stage the PMKs ===")
  PrintNl()
  UartDrain()
  Line("tick hz          ", g_hz)

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  The settings text. Find the end by scanning for the NUL the `fill`
  ;  left behind, and REFUSE rather than guess if there is not one in
  ;  the window: parsing 8 KB of unknown DRAM as a settings file
  ;  reports a syntax error on a line that is not in the file, which
  ;  sends somebody to edit a file that is perfectly correct.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  setLen = -1
  For i = 0 To #SET_WIN - 1
    If PeekA(#SET_ADDR + i) = 0
      setLen = i
      Break
    EndIf
  Next
  If setLen < 0
    UartWriteStr("  NO TERMINATOR in 8 KB at $01400000. Type:")
    PrintNl()
    UartWriteStr("    fill 1400000 0 800")
    PrintNl()
    UartWriteStr("    load SETTINGS.TXT 1400000")
    PrintNl()
    UartWriteStr("=== stopped at the settings ===")
    PrintNl()
    ProcedureReturn 1
  EndIf
  Line("settings bytes   ", setLen)

  ok = SettingsParse(#SET_ADDR, setLen)
  Line("SettingsParse (want 1)", ok)
  If ok = 0
    UartWriteStr("  ")
    UartWriteStr(SettingsErrorText())
    PrintNl()
    Line("  at file line   ", SettingsErrorLine())
    UartWriteStr("=== stopped at the settings ===")
    PrintNl()
    ProcedureReturn 1
  EndIf

  fp = Fnv1a(#SET_ADDR, setLen)
  UartWriteStr("  settings fingerprint  $")
  PutHexN(fp, 8)
  PrintNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  What is already staged, if anything, and is it still valid?
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  count = 0
  If Rd32(#PMKS_ADDR) = #PMKS_MAGIC
    oldFp = Rd32(#PMKS_ADDR + #PMKS_OFF_FP)
    If oldFp = fp
      count = Rd32(#PMKS_ADDR + #PMKS_OFF_COUNT)
      If count < 0 Or count > #PMKS_MAX
        count = 0
      EndIf
      Line("already staged   ", count)
    Else
      UartWriteStr("  the staged window was built from a DIFFERENT SETTINGS.TXT")
      PrintNl()
      UartWriteStr("  ($")
      PutHexN(oldFp, 8)
      UartWriteStr(") - discarding it and starting again.")
      PrintNl()
    EndIf
  Else
    UartWriteStr("  nothing staged yet")
    PrintNl()
  EndIf

  ; The magic goes DOWN only at the end of a run. While derivations are
  ; in progress the window must not look valid, because a deadman reset
  ; partway through would otherwise leave a count that overstates what
  ; is in it.
  Wr32(#PMKS_ADDR, 0)
  Wr32(#PMKS_ADDR + #PMKS_OFF_COUNT, count)
  Wr32(#PMKS_ADDR + #PMKS_OFF_FP, fp)
  Wr32(#PMKS_ADDR + 12, 0)

  PrintNl()
  UartWriteStr("-- derivations --")
  PrintNl()
  UartDrain()

  usable = 0
  derived = 0
  owed = 0
  slot = SettingsWifiNextSlot(0)
  While slot <> 0
    ssid    = SettingsWifiSlotSsid(slot)
    ssidLen = SettingsLength(SettingsWifiSlotSsidKey(slot))
    pass    = SettingsWifiSlotPassword(slot)
    passLen = SettingsLength(SettingsWifiSlotPasswordKey(slot))

    If ssid = 0 Or ssidLen < 1 Or ssidLen > 32 Or pass = 0 Or passLen < 8 Or passLen > 63
      UartWriteStr("  slot ")
      PrintDec(slot)
      UartWriteStr("  ")
      PrintSsid(ssid, ssidLen)
      UartWriteStr("   SKIPPED - not a usable credential (pass bytes ")
      PrintDec(passLen)
      UartWriteStr(")")
      PrintNl()
      UartDrain()
    Else
      usable = usable + 1
      If AlreadyStaged(count, ssid, ssidLen) = 1
        UartWriteStr("  slot ")
        PrintDec(slot)
        UartWriteStr("  ")
        PrintSsid(ssid, ssidLen)
        UartWriteStr("   already staged")
        PrintNl()
        UartDrain()
      ElseIf count >= #PMKS_MAX
        owed = owed + 1
        UartWriteStr("  slot ")
        PrintDec(slot)
        UartWriteStr("   NO ROOM - raise PMKS_MAX")
        PrintNl()
        UartDrain()
      ElseIf MsSince(tRun) > #PMKS_START_BY_MS
        owed = owed + 1
        UartWriteStr("  slot ")
        PrintDec(slot)
        UartWriteStr("  ")
        PrintSsid(ssid, ssidLen)
        UartWriteStr("   DEFERRED - too late in the budget to start one")
        PrintNl()
        UartDrain()
      Else
        UartWriteStr("  slot ")
        PrintDec(slot)
        UartWriteStr("  ")
        PrintSsid(ssid, ssidLen)
        UartWriteStr("   pass bytes ")
        PrintDec(passLen)
        UartWriteStr("   deriving ...")
        PrintNl()
        UartDrain()

        ent = #PMKS_ADDR + #PMKS_HDR + count * #PMKS_ENTRY
        For i = 0 To #PMKS_ENTRY - 1
          PokeB(ent + i, 0)
        Next

        t = Ticks()
        ok = Wpa2Psk(pass, passLen, ssid, ssidLen, ent + #PMKS_OFF_PMK)
        took = MsSince(t)

        If ok <> 32
          UartWriteStr("     Wpa2Psk REFUSED, returned ")
          PrintDec(ok)
          PrintNl()
          UartDrain()
          For i = 0 To #PMKS_ENTRY - 1
            PokeB(ent + i, 0)
          Next
          owed = owed + 1
        Else
          Wr32(ent + #PMKS_OFF_SLOT, slot)
          Wr32(ent + #PMKS_OFF_SLEN, ssidLen)
          For i = 0 To ssidLen - 1
            PokeB(ent + #PMKS_OFF_SSID + i, PeekA(ssid + i))
          Next
          count = count + 1
          derived = derived + 1
          UartWriteStr("     PMK derived in ")
          PrintDec(took)
          UartWriteStr(" ms")
          PrintNl()
          UartDrain()
          Wr32(#PMKS_ADDR + #PMKS_OFF_COUNT, count)
        EndIf
      EndIf
    EndIf

    slot = SettingsWifiNextSlot(slot)
  Wend

  ; The header last, so a run that reset partway leaves no magic.
  Wr32(#PMKS_ADDR + #PMKS_OFF_COUNT, count)
  If count > 0
    Wr32(#PMKS_ADDR, #PMKS_MAGIC)
  EndIf

  ; The library's own key material, gone. The staged copy is deliberate
  ; and is the point; these are the working buffers.
  Pbkdf2Wipe()

  PrintNl()
  Line("usable networks  ", usable)
  Line("staged now       ", count)
  Line("derived this run ", derived)
  Line("still owed       ", owed)
  Line("start-by ms      ", #PMKS_START_BY_MS)
  Line("elapsed ms       ", MsSince(tRun))
  UartWriteStr("  window at $")
  PutHexN(#PMKS_ADDR, 8)
  PrintNl()
  If owed > 0
    UartWriteStr("=== RUN THIS AGAIN - ")
    PrintDec(owed)
    UartWriteStr(" still to derive ===")
    PrintNl()
    UartDrain()
    ProcedureReturn 2
  EndIf
  If count = 0
    UartWriteStr("=== nothing staged ===")
    PrintNl()
    UartDrain()
    ProcedureReturn 1
  EndIf
  UartWriteStr("=== all staged - now run the join ===")
  PrintNl()
  UartDrain()
  ProcedureReturn 0
EndProcedure

Main()
